                       SETS
DEFINITION

  collection of Well defined and distinct object is known as set.
   ex: {1,2,3} , {x,y,z}

  Thats why SETS cant contain same object twice.
   ex: {x,x,y,z} is NOT a set 

  positions of element inside the paranthesis doesnt matter.
   ex {x,z,y} = {x,y,z}
 
  collection of subjective element are NOT sets 
   ex; {collection of most attractive female}
    beauty standard may vary over person to person , thus this collection NOT distinct.


_______________________________________________________________________________________
BASIC CONCEPT        
 A set is generally denoted by a capital alphabet.
 ex; A = {x.3.f ...}

 The alphabet inside a set would be denoted in smaller case.
 ex: A = {a,b,c}

 if 'a' belongs to A(set) then we can denoted it as
 ex: a∈A                              (here ∈ is  "belongs to " symbol)

 if 'a' does not belongs to A(set) then we can denoted it as :
 ex: a∉A     

______________________________________________________________________________________

Symbol knowledge : 
 ∀ means "for all"
 :,| means "such that"
 , means "and"
 ∃ means "there exist"

