TYPE OF SETS 

 FINITE SET : number of element in a set are finite.
  ex: {1,2,3,4,5,6}
 INFINITE SET : number of element in a set are infinite.
  ex: {x∈N, x <0 }
 NULL , EMPTY , VOID SET :  a set having no element in it.
  ex: F = {x, x∈R ,x^2 + 2 = 0}   
      F = {}
      F = Φ              (symbol of Phi)
 SINGLETON SET :  a set with a single element.
 ex :  A = {1}
 EQUAL SET : sets having same element in it.
  ex: A = {1,3,2},B =  [3,2,1]
 EQUIVALENT SETS: sets having same cardinal number.
  ex: C = {1,23,4}  , D= {1,6,4}

________________________________________________________________________________________

INTERVAL

 OPEN INTERVAL : condition not including the number used
  ex: {x:x∈N,1<x<3 } (here 1,3 are not included)
      (1,3)
      now set will be A = {2}

 CLOSED INTERVAL : condition  including the number used
  ex: {x:x∈N,1≤x≤3 } (here 1,3 are  included)
      [1,3]
      now set wil be A={1,2,3}
 SEMI CLOSED INTERVAL : condition including one number used
  ex: {x:x∈N,1<x≤3}
      (1,3]
       now set will be A={2,3}

