SUBSET
 
 sets formed from elements of a parent sets is known as subset
  ex: A= {1,2,3} 
        B ={}
         {1}
         {2}
         {3}
         {1,2}
         {3,1}
         {2,3}
         {1,2,3}
  therefore, B⊆A             (⊆ means "subset of")
 number of subset = 2^n(A)
  for ex:
   A = {1,2,9}
   n(A) = 3 
   therefore, no of possible subset = 2^3= 8
 every set is a SUBSET of itself.(therefore we used ⊆)
  if same set is not inculded then we use "⊂" sign.
  as known as proper subset
 EMPTY set is subset of every set. 

 Proper Subset 
  all subset except the same set:
  ex A={1,2}
   B = {},{1},{2}
   therfore B⊂A
  proper subset = 2^(n(a)) - 1
_______________________________________________________________________________________

POWER SET 
 set of subsets is known as Power set.
  ex: A = {a,b,c}
  P(A)= {{},{a},{b},{c},{a,b},{b,a},{a,c},{abc}}

