Universal set 
 set that contain all the sets under consideration, denoted by U, its also super set of all sets.
 ex:
  A = {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8}
  B = {1,2,6}
  C = {1,2}
  D = [1,7,8]
  THERE A is here Universal set 
______________________________________________________________________________________

Disjoint Set: sets with no common element or no intersection 
 ex: A = {1,2,3} , B = {q,w,e}
  so A∩B = {} or Φ 
______________________________________________________________________________________
 
Operation on sets


 COMPLEMENT: distinct element in univeral set compared to subset
  ex : U = {1,2,f,3,4}
   A = {1,3,f}
   Aᶜ = {4,2}
  MORE INFO:
   (Aᶜ)ᶜ = A 
   Uᶜ = {}
   {}ᶜ= U 
   n(A) + n(Aᶜ) = U
 UNION: to add sets.
  ex: A = {1,2,d,5}
   B={7,6,4}
   AUB= {1,2,4,5,6,7,d}
 INTERSECTION :common elements between set.
  ex: A = {1,2,3}
  B={3,2,4,5}
  A∩B = {3,2}
 DIFFERENCE: 
  ex: A = {1,2,3,4,5}
   B = {3,4,5,6,7}
   A-B = {1,2}
   B-A ={6,7}
 SYMMETRIC DIFFERENCE: union of difference of two set .
 ex: A= {q,w,e} , B= {e,r,t}
  (A-B)U(B-A)

